  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "big beat's arrangement move, as a drum part: four bars of the break, two bars where the drums drop out, and two bars of a snare roll doubling back in to the drop",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Eight bars on the theme clock: the break over a four for four bars, nothing but the composer's own parts for two, then the kick on the beats under a snare roll in eighths and then sixteenths, rising, back into bar one. It is a section move written as a cell: a track pin plays it in every drummed section, so the drop-out lands where the eight-bar clock puts it and not where the arrangement's drop is — the gap is section-scoped cells."
  }
